```

## Expected behavior

Run `next` in command line. You will not see any linting errors.

If however you make a `pages/_app.js` file and put in a code error there, you will see a corresponding eslint error in the console. So eslint works on `pages/_app.js`, but not on any files (unless you run `next build`).

