# Feature request
Allow `getStaticPaths` function to return extra properties per path. 

## Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.
Some headless CMS solutions use an ID as only method for retrieving individual content. If you want to use a SLUG for the path there is no way to pass said ID to the `getStaticProps` function, only the SLUG gets passed. Any extra properties are not. 

Ex: `/partner/[slug].tsx`
```typescript
export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const res = await client.getEntries<IPortalFields>({ content_type: 'portal' })
  const paths = res.items.map(item => ({
    params: { slug: item.fields.slug, id: item.sys.id }
  }))
  return { paths, fallback: false }
}
export async function getStaticProps({ params }) {
  const res = await client.getEntry<IPortalFields>(params.id)
  return {
    props: {
      partner: {
        slug: res.fields.slug,
        company: res.fields.companyName,
        logo: res.fields.logo.fields.file.url
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This will not work because the ID is not passed to the `getStaticProps` function only the SLUG is passed.

## Describe the solution you'd like

Allow `getStaticPath` to return extra properties. Could also be as part of a different property per path, like `props` this would also allow typing on it. 

```typescript
interface PageProps {
  id: string
}

export async function getStaticPaths<PageProps>() {
  const res = await client.getEntries<IPortalFields>({ content_type: 'portal' })
  const paths = res.items.map(item => ({
    params: { uid: item.fields.uid },
    props: { id: item.sys.id }
  }))
  return { paths, fallback: false }
}
export async function getStaticProps<PageProps>({ params, props }) {
  const res = await client.getEntry<IPortalFields>(props.id)
  return {
    props: {
      partner: {
        uid: res.fields.uid,
        company: res.fields.companyName,
        logo: res.fields.logo.fields.file.url
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Describe alternatives you've considered

The only solution I found so far is to write a JSON map of this extra properties to a file on the `getStaticPaths` function and retrieve it on the `getStaticProps` function

